ce.\n- Intellectual merit: Low novelty. The approach (API interception + centralized immutable logging) is well-established in distributed systems engineering.\n- Broader scientific impact: Indirect at best. It might free up researcher time from compliance concerns, but that's a resource allocation benefit, not a scientific impact per se.\n\nI'll reject this with a low promise score. It's competent engineering but doesn't clear the bar for intellectual merit or knowledge advancement.\n",
