es multiple articles of the AI Act simultaneously. The promise score should be high - maybe 82-85. Not 100 because there are real implementation risks (data governance for training, the tool itself needing its own documentation/compliance pathway, risk of over-reliance on automated detection for legally nuanced determinations). But it's clearly worth pursuing.\n\nLet me settle on a score: I'll go with 84. It strongly serves compliance objectives but has some manageable risks that prevent a near-perfect score from my vantage point.\n",
