rsion-controlled audit trail via MLflow/DVC) is proportionate to the regulatory need. I'd approve this with some reservations about scope creep into risk assessment automation, but as written it's a sensible, cost-effective approach to meeting Article 12 and Recital 71 requirements.\n\nPromise score: I think around 68-72. It's a solid, efficient proposal that uses existing tools well, but the \"real-time\" and \"risk assessments in real time\" elements introduce unnecessary complexity for marginal regulatory benefit, and there are hidden operational costs in researcher workflow changes. Not a slam-dunk 90+ because of those inefficiencies, but clearly above the reject threshold because the core approach is resource-efficient and proportionate.\n\nI'll go with 70.\n",
