l it serves institutional survival and regulatory compliance — I'd say around 85-90. It's not perfect (the \"universal\" framing could be too reductive for different risk categories, and lifetime coverage beyond deployment needs explicit confirmation), but the architectural direction is exactly right and it reduces systemic compliance risk significantly.\n\nI'll give it an 87 — strong approval with minor reservations about scope completeness for all Article 12 sub-clauses and post-market operational logging.\n",
