ng framework is a strong signal of serious compliance posture.\n- From institutional survival: failure to comply with Article 12 for high-risk systems could result in penalties up to €35M or 7% of global turnover under the EU AI Act's enforcement provisions. Having this built-in systematically reduces that risk dramatically.\n\nThis is a strong, well-scoped proposal that directly addresses regulatory requirements. I would approve it. The promise score should be high — perhaps 82-88. It's not a 100 because it's still at the conceptual level and there are implementation details (particularly around Annex III point 1(a) specific minimums, lifetime duration of logs, storage security, etc.) that need to be worked out. But as a proposal to commit resources to build this framework, it clears my bar decisively.\n\nI'll give it an 85.\n",
