t anyway, so the cost would be incurred regardless; centralizing it just makes it cheaper in aggregate. The risk of \"slowing down research\" is mitigated by the plug-and-play design.\n\nI think this clears my bar. It's a well-structured use of existing resources to meet a mandatory requirement efficiently. My concern is scope creep and whether the \"lab-wide\" framing matches actual need (how many high-risk projects do we actually have?), but that's an implementation detail, not a fundamental flaw in the approach.\n\nPromise score: I'd say around 72-78. It's clearly good from my vantage point — efficient use of existing infrastructure, prevents duplication, addresses a mandatory requirement. But it's somewhat generic and doesn't address the specific logging requirements per Article 12(2) and (3), which means there will be additional work beyond just \"event recording.\" Also, \"lab-wide\" might be over-scoped if only a few projects are actually high-risk. I'll go with 74.\n\nDecision: approve.\n",
