        "content": "{\n  \"screenings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P1900\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Article 12(2) does not merely obligate us to store logs; it requires that logging capabilities *enable* the identification of risk situations (Art. 79(1)), facilitate post-market monitoring (Art. 72), and support operational oversight (Art. 26(5)). An automated analytics layer over those same mandatory logs is, in effect, the operational fulfilment of those enabling duties—without it we would be archiving data while remaining blind to drift or emerging risk triggers, leaving us exposed to enforcement and market-trust consequences. The proposal also reuses infrastructure we must build regardless, keeping marginal cost modest while strengthening our demonstrable compliance posture before regulators.\",\n      \"decision\": \"approve\",\n      \"promise\": 87\n    }\n  ]\n}",
