e classification step, creates accountability through dual-reviewer model, provides recurring cadence, and explicitly links to Article 12 requirements. I'd say around 82-85. It's not a 90+ because it's somewhat generic in its language and doesn't address edge cases (mid-quarter reclassification, substantial modification triggers, what constitutes \"mapping features against Article 12\" operationally). But it's clearly something I would back without much hesitation.\n\nI'll go with 83.\n",
