om my vantage point. It uses existing infrastructure efficiently, reduces ongoing operational costs, has a clear trigger mechanism that doesn't disrupt research workflows, and addresses a real compliance requirement (Recital 71 documentation currency). The main risk is metadata completeness, but that's a manageable implementation detail rather than a fundamental flaw. I would approve this.\n\nPromise score: This is very well-aligned with my mandate. It's efficient, leverages existing infrastructure, bounded in scope, and addresses a genuine compliance need with low ongoing resource drain. I'd say around 82-85. The slight deduction is for the metadata completeness risk and the fact that it doesn't fully cover Article 12's logging requirements (it's more Recital 71 documentation than Article 12 event logging). But within its stated scope, it's excellent.\n\nI'll go with 83.\n",
