ved from a compliance standpoint. It's not perfect (doesn't explicitly detail retention, GDPR interplay, or the specific Annex III point 1(a) fields), but as an institutional framework initiative, it's exactly the kind of structural investment that a compliance officer would want to see. The \"mandated for use\" aspect is particularly important — without it, compliance becomes voluntary and unreliable.\n\nI'd approve this. Promise score: I'd say around 82-85. It's strongly aligned with my mandate but has some gaps (GDPR data protection in logging, explicit mention of retention periods, the specific Art. 12(3) fields for biometric systems). But the core architecture is right and it addresses the fundamental obligation systematically.\n\nLet me settle on 84.\n",
