rs my bar at a moderate level. It's technically viable, addresses a real engineering constraint (logging overhead), and if scoped well, produces reusable components. But it's research, not immediate prototyping value. I'd approve it with a moderate promise score - maybe 62-68. It's useful but indirect for my specific function.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise 63. The technical problem is real and solvable, the outputs would benefit our prototyping pipeline, but it's an indirect contribution and \"research\" carries inherent schedule risk from a prototyping-speed perspective.\n",
